\section{Normalization and Clamping}

To ensure stability, UFSL components are normalized:
\[
\Theta_{norm}(t) =
\frac{\Theta(t)}{\|\Theta(t)\| + \epsilon},
\]
where $\epsilon$ prevents division by zero.

Clamping ensures:
\[
\Theta_{clamp}(t) =
\min\left(\Theta_{norm}(t), \Theta_{\max}\right).
\]

This prevents:
\begin{itemize}
    \item latent-force explosion,
    \item structural collapse,
    \item metabolic overload,
    \item continuity degradation.
\end{itemize}

